## Decisions Made
- Skill name `applying-coding-baseline` (gerund pattern): chosen over `supplementing-agent-directives` to avoid trigger ambiguity with `guarding-agent-directives`
- Skip `guarding-agent-directives` verification on insertion: the curated set is pre-vetted by construction; user authority preserved via per-rule opt-out at Step 4
- On duplicate detection: REPLACE with canonical wording (not insert-only): user requirement to normalize ad-hoc rules across projects
- Data-driven extension via `reference/baseline-rules.md`: new rules added by appending a `## Rule N` section, no code changes needed
- Started with 4 rules, expanded to 6: Rule 5 (Fail Fast vs Graceful Handling) and Rule 6 (Documentation Priority) added on user request after initial implementation
- Generalize framework-specific wording (Rails / YARD): replace with framework-neutral terms ("API doc comments at class/module/function level") and keep tool-specific names only as detection keywords (javadoc, doxygen, jsdoc, docstring)
- Keep existing "No error handling for impossible scenarios" alongside new "No over-defending" bullet: removing the original would drop detection-keyword coverage for projects that already have it phrased that way

## Problems Encountered
- skill-creator's `aggregate_benchmark.py` expects `eval-N/<config>/run-1/grading.json` directory layout; my evals were at `eval-N/<config>/grading.json`. Resolved by writing `benchmark.json` directly using the documented schema in `references/schemas.md`.
- Eval 3 (already-canonical) was non-discriminating: both configurations correctly skipped because the test prompt explicitly contained "only change what's needed". Noted as a limitation in benchmark.json analyst notes.
- Eval 2 with-skill changed section ordering when applying replacements (moved "Use existing libraries" to before the new section). All assertions still passed but exact layout preservation could be tightened in a follow-up iteration.

## Constraints Identified
- Directive content (CLAUDE.md / AGENTS.md / referenced docs) must be in English: project policy stated in AGENTS.md and user memory
- Reference files over 100 lines should include a table of contents at the top: per skill-creator's `reference/structure.md`
- macOS shells without GNU coreutils need `gtimeout` (Homebrew) instead of `timeout`: skill-creator's shipping-pr workflow detects and falls back
- The skill must coexist with `guarding-agent-directives` without invoking it: justified in SKILL.md "Skipping verification" section

