## Context
Created `plugins/skill-set/skills/applying-coding-baseline/`, a new skill that inserts a curated set of behavioral discipline rules into coding agent directive files. Files: `SKILL.md` (120 lines), `reference/baseline-rules.md` (258 lines), with `AGENTS.md` updated to register the skill. Validation: ran a 3-case skill-creator eval loop with 6 parallel subagents (3 with-skill, 3 baseline), giving 100% pass rate with-skill vs 46% baseline. Validated against `creating-skills` checklist (one issue found and fixed: missing TOC on a >100-line reference file). Iterated twice to add Rules 5 and 6 with framework-neutral wording. Outcome: completed and ready for PR.

